  unlockCluesOnComplete:
  - clueId: L08_LotusLeaf_Ratio
    title: Lotus Leaf - Ratio Clue
    content: Lotus leaf works best as a very low-ratio fresh accent.
    relatedIngredients:
    - {fileID: 1623195174}
    relatedDimension: 2
  - clueId: L08_LotusLeaf_Combination
    title: Lotus Leaf - Combination Clue
    content: Lotus leaf can be carried by glutinous rice, but it should not be ground
      with strong aromas like black sesame.
    relatedIngredients:
    - {fileID: 1623195174}
    relatedDimension: 3
  - clueId: L08_LotusLeaf_Order
    title: Lotus Leaf - Order Clue
    content: Lotus leaf works best at the end. Early or heavy handling removes its
      fresh aroma.
    relatedIngredients:
    - {fileID: 1623195174}
    relatedDimension: 1
  processFeedbackRules: []
  fallbackHintText: No new experiment conclusion is available yet. Keep the parts
    that are already correct and adjust only one uncertain mechanic at a time.
  progressiveHintRules:
  - ruleId: L08_Hint_RedBean_Ratio
    priority: 22
    mechanic: 2
    hintText: Red bean should form the thickest base note, higher than glutinous
      rice, sesame, and lotus leaf.
  - ruleId: L08_Hint_LotusLeaf_Ratio
    priority: 21
    mechanic: 2
    hintText: Lotus leaf is a light finishing aroma. Keep it at the lowest ratio.
  - ruleId: L08_Hint_Rice_Lotus_Combination
    priority: 20
    mechanic: 3
    hintText: Glutinous rice can carry the lotus-leaf aroma. Put glutinous rice and
      lotus leaf in the same group.
  - ruleId: L08_Hint_Sesame_Lotus_Combination
    priority: 19
    mechanic: 3
    hintText: Black sesame is too strong and can bury lotus leaf. Keep them separate.
  - ruleId: L08_Hint_RedBean_Order
    priority: 22
    mechanic: 1
    hintText: Red bean should build the base first. Put red bean in the first position.
  - ruleId: L08_Hint_LotusLeaf_Order
    priority: 21
    mechanic: 1
    hintText: Lotus leaf is fragile and should appear last.
  - ruleId: L08_Hint_Middle_Order
    priority: 20
    mechanic: 1
    hintText: After red bean, let glutinous rice form body before adding a small
      amount of black sesame.
  successFeedback: Red bean forms the base, glutinous rice supports the body, black
    sesame adds tail depth, and lotus leaf lifts the finish.
  closeFeedback: The steamed rice direction appears, but lotus leaf, sesame, or red
    bean needs a more accurate role.
  wrongFeedback: Lotus leaf is crushed, or black sesame steals the main body.
