    priority: 21
    mechanic: 3
    hintText: White pepper, peanut, and dried tangerine peel release differently.
      Try handling them as separate groups.
  - ruleId: L07_Hint_Pepper_Peel
    priority: 20
    mechanic: 3
    hintText: Grinding white pepper with dried tangerine peel can make spice and
      bitterness rush out together. Separate them.
  successFeedback: White pepper stays clear without choking, peanut keeps warmth,
    and dried peel finishes lightly.
  closeFeedback: The aroma direction is close, but some ingredients still interfere
    with each other.
  wrongFeedback: White pepper is too harsh, or dried peel bitterness suppresses the
    warm peanut note.
